# User-Scoped Multi-Tenant Data Isolation

This plan outlines the steps required to isolate data on a per-user basis. All transactional and master data (Products, Categories, Warehouses, Suppliers, Customers, Sales, Expenses, Loans, Staff, and Settings) will be scoped to the logged-in user. When a user logs in, they will only see and modify their own data.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> **Database Schema Migration**: Adding `userId` as a relation to existing models in a SQLite database with existing records can require database migration. We propose making `userId` optional (`String?`) or automatically running a script to assign existing records to the first registered user during the migration phase, which avoids database reset. If database reset is acceptable, we can run `prisma migrate dev` directly.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Authentication Check**: All API routes in `app.js` (except login/register) are already protected by the `protect` middleware. We will use the `req.user.id` injected by this middleware to associate and filter all data queries.

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - Should we associate all existing unassociated records with the first user in the database, or is resetting the database (`dev.db`) acceptable? (If this is a local development environment, a reset is easiest).

